  "result": "Perfect! All 258 tests pass. I've successfully implemented the VAT summary report:\n\n**Added vatSummary(invoices) to src/reports.js:**\n- Returns array [{ rate, base, vat }] for each VAT rate found\n- Filters invoices: status 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid' (excludes draft)\n- For each line in qualifying invoices:\n  - Calculates base: line amount after discount (qty \u00d7 unitPrice - discount)\n  - Calculates VAT: base \u00d7 rate / 100, rounded per line\n- Aggregates by VAT rate across all lines and invoices\n- Sorts by rate descending (highest VAT rate first)\n- Does not mutate input invoices\n\n**Added 18 comprehensive tests covering:**\n- Empty invoices list\n- No issued/paid invoices (excludes draft)\n- Invoice status filtering (issued, partially_paid, paid included; draft excluded)\n- Correct base calculation (after discount)\n- Correct VAT calculation per line\n- Zero VAT rate (0%)\n- Missing vatRate (defaults to 0)\n- Multiple lines with same VAT rate (aggregates correctly)\n- Multiple lines with different VAT rates (separates correctly)\n- Sorting by rate descending\n- Aggregation across multiple invoices\n- Discounts on multiple lines\n- Mixed invoice statuses in one call\n- Complex scenario with multiple rates, quantities, and discounts\n- Input immutability\n\nExample output:\n```javascript\nvatSummary([...invoices])\n// [\n//   { rate: 21, base: 95000, vat: 19950 },\n//   { rate: 6, base: 10000, vat: 600 },\n//   { rate: 0, base: 10000, vat: 0 }\n// ]\n```\n\nAll 258 tests passing.",
